” Maximizing ROI with the Expertise of a Digital Marketing Agency — “What sets this digital marketing agency apart is their commitment to transparency and collaboration. They keep us informed every step of the way.”\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"228\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:37\" name=\"Footer\" x=\"0\" y=\"339\" width=\"420\" height=\"315\">\n          <text id=\"3:38\" name=\"Footer\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:39\" name=\"Logo_MAC · “We offer a comprehensive suite of digital marketing services that cover all aspects of your online presence. From SEO and social media marketing to content creation and PPC advertising, we have the expertise and resources to handle your diverse marketing needs.” Social: Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_LinkedIn · Logo_Instagram Navigation: Service · Agency · Case Study · Resources · Contact Licence: Privacy Policy · Copyright · Email Address Contact: (406) 555-0120 (Icon_Phone) · hey@example.com (Icon_Mail) · 2972 Westheimer Rd. Santa Ana, Illinois 85486 (Icon_Map_Pin)\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"247\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:40\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"64\" y=\"2603\" width=\"1312\" height=\"312\">\n      <text id=\"3:41\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"328\" height=\"35\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:42\" name=\"Fixed vs yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"261\">\n        <frame id=\"3:43\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"201\">\n          <text id=\"3:44\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"3:45\" name=\"• Frame name • Must-include content (what, not how) • All data and copy • Brand colors #99EA48 and #010205, and Plus Jakarta Sans • Media: logo, social logos, icons • Default Button\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"120\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:46\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"261\">\n          <text id=\"3:47\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"197\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"3:48\" name=\"• Layout, grid, grouping, order and emphasis of every section • All other colors: neutrals, text, light / dark section backgrounds, surfaces, borders, chart and progress colors, selected filter, error / disabled • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation • All states: current filter, card hover, expanded / collapsed FAQ, hover • Header with dropdown triggers, stat and chart cards, client wordmark row, video block, filter tags, case-study card, testimonial with pager, FAQ accordion, article card, CTA banner, footer • How image placeholders are sized and placed\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"180\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:49\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"64\" y=\"2963\" width=\"1312\" height=\"259\">\n      <text id=\"3:50\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"222\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:51\" name=\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <text id=\"3:52\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Information hierarchy across sections 4. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 5. Component reuse 6. State design (current filter, card hover, expanded FAQ)\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"132\" />\n      <text id=\"3:53\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 1 named frame, your components.\" x=\"0\" y=\"237\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not call get_design_context, the agent will not be able to implement the design."}],"_meta":{"mcpRequestId":"ae5b897a-e40b-4967-a43e-28bd7e90ae74"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LHNO5CUkvXMdWbHC620jPk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FCnWpF1ytfKUZFG3CDrKtY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n {\n  \"i\": \"3:4\",\n  \"n\": \"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\",\n  \"t\": \"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\",\n  \"fs\": 13,\n  \"f\": {\n   \"family\": \"Inter\",\n   \"style\": \"Bold\",\n   \"variationSettings\": {\n    \"wght\": 700,\n    \"slnt\": 0\n   }\n  },\n  \"w\": 182\n },\n {\n  \"i\": \"3:5\",\n  \"n\": \"MAC — digital marketing agency landing page\",\n  \"t\": \"MAC — digital marketing agency landing page\",\n  \"fs\": 36,\n  \"f\": {\n   \"family\": \"Inter\",\n   \"style\": \"Bold\",\n   \"variationSettings\": {\n    \"wght\": 700,\n    \"slnt\": 0\n   }\n  },\n  \"w\": 1312\n },\n {\n  \"i\": \"3:6\",\n  \"n\": \"Design the landing page of a digital marketing agency: introduce the agency, prove results, show case studies, answer common questions and invite visitors to get in touch. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\",\n  \"t\": \"Design the landing page of a digital marketing agency: introduce the agency, prove results, show case studies, answer common questions and invite visitors to get in touch. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\",\n  \"fs\": 17,\n  \"f\": {\n   \"family\": \"Inter\",\n   \"style\": \"Regular\",\n   \"variationSettings\": {\n    \"wght\": 400,\n    \"slnt\": 0\n   }\n  },\n  \"w\": 1312\n },\n {\n  \"i\": \"3:8\",\n  \"n\": \"How to work\",\n  \"t\": \"How to work\",\n  \"fs\": 24,\n  \"f\": {\n   \"family\": \"Inter\",\n   \"style\": \"Bold\",\n   \"variationSettings\": {\n    \"wght\": 700,\n    \"slnt\": 0\n   }\n  },\n  \"w\": 147\n },\n {\n  \"i\": \"3:9\",\n  \"n\": \"1. Build exactly the 1 frame below, named exactly as listed. It is a single landing page, so there is no prototype to wire. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the logo, the social logos and the icons from 04 · Media. The source has no photography: case-study thumbnails, the video poster and the avatars are image placeholders — keep them as placeholders. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\",\n  \"t\": \"1. Build exactly the 1 frame below, named exactly as listed. It is a single landing page, so there is no prototype to wire.\\n2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions.\\n3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently.\\n4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\\n5. Use the logo, the social logos and the icons from 04 · Media. The source has no photography: case-study thumbnails, the video poster and the avatars are image placeholders — keep them as placeholders.\\n6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\",\n  \"fs\": 15,\n  \"f\": {\n   \"fam